        {
          "path": "_m/w/w/y/h/lushun-museum-wp/at-the-green-bower-hermitage-m.png",
          "filename": "\"At the Green Bower Hermitage Miaoyu asks the planchette (fuji) about a Jade\" (栊翠庵妙玉扶乩玉) - scene from Dream of the Red Chamber. 19th century painting by Sun Wen.png",
          "caption": "According to Elena Valussi (2023), \"Spirit writing and gender in Chinese religious practice\", Loyola University Chicago ([1], from 26 minutes onwards), the painting depicts to the right the characters Miaoyu and Xiuwen practicing spirit writing (fuji) with a basket, while helpers to the left are recording what is supposed to be the words of the Immortal who gives the spiritual response: he is identified as the man in the top right part of the painting, above a cloud",
          "alt": "According to Elena Valussi (2023), \"Spirit writing and gender in Chinese religious practice\", Loyola University Chicago ([1], from 26 minutes onwards), the painting depicts to the right the characters Miaoyu and Xiuwen practicing spirit writing (fuji) with a basket, while helpers to the left are recording what is supposed to be the words of the Immortal who gives the spiritual response: he is identified as the man in the top right part of the painting, above a cloud",
